We have the big question, what
is an API, the definition for an

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:57.600
API is Application Programming
Interface. But that is not

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:02.610
explanatory. In simple words,
API is responsible for

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:07.050
transmitting the data. Or
rather, it is a way for multiple

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:12.150
applications to communicate with
each other. In today's

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:17.670
technology driven world, we are
connected like never before. API

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:22.050
is the critical engine behind
sharing information across

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:27.450
multiple application, and
programming. APA is responsible

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:31.050
for getting a request from the
client, and then sending a

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:35.490
response back to the client
based on the request, and the

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:39.420
request and response that will
be multiple of them. And it

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:44.430
continues. So basically, if a
client is looking for some data,

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:49.350
it would ask API by sending a
request. And then EPA would

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:54.660
return back that data in form of
a response. The model that we

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:58.740
see here is the website model.
What is different between that

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:03.570
and an API, what makes an API
stand out is it is not just the

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:08.160
web browser that can call an
API, many other application can

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:13.080
invoke an API endpoint. So let's
say you have an API that can be

